{
 "id": "2026-11-11-a",
 "title": "All 8 billion humans fit in a sugar cube 🧊",
 "description": "Atoms are almost entirely empty space: blow one up to a football stadium and the nucleus is a marble on the centre spot. Squeeze that space out of every person on Earth and humanity shrinks to roughly a sugar cube (a few cubic centimetres), which would still weigh hundreds of millions of tonnes. You never fall through your chair because electrons push each other away.\n\nSources: https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/follow-up-the-volume-of-humanity-if-all-the-space-in-our-atoms-is-removed ; https://www.fnal.gov/pub/today/archive/archive_2013/today13-12-06_NutshellReadMore.html ; https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-3/pages/10-1-properties-of-nuclei ; https://bigthink.com/starts-with-a-bang/matter-mostly-empty-space/ ; https://zmescience.com/ecology/world-problems/world-human-population-mass-287-million-tonnes-432432",
